WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.605
27 pages.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.774
That's one house type
from one housebuilder.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:12.322
Elevations, floor plans, the foundation
plan, the electrics, the tiling.

00:00:12.961 --> 00:00:15.248
Three of them matter for scaffold.

00:00:15.654 --> 00:00:17.767
The estimator finds those three.

00:00:18.232 --> 00:00:21.227
Then they hunt for the right
dimension among a dozen.

00:00:21.691 --> 00:00:25.128
Twice the length, twice
the width, add the corners,

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:28.019
times four lifts, times the rate.

00:00:28.646 --> 00:00:29.784
In pencil first.

00:00:30.248 --> 00:00:34.718
Then typed again, line by line,
into the estimating system.

00:00:35.345 --> 00:00:40.975
On the foundation plan,
one line reads 12,170.

00:00:41.521 --> 00:00:44.214
It's the diagonal check, not the wall.

00:00:44.853 --> 00:00:48.963
Read it as the length, and the
quote is short by 6.5 metres.

00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:52.411
£157 on one plot.

00:00:52.957 --> 00:00:56.753
Across a 40-plot phase, over £6,000,

00:00:56.939 --> 00:00:59.493
given away before the
first tube goes up.

00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:02.384
This is Drawing-to-Quote Engine.

00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:04.114
Give it the whole pack.

00:01:04.752 --> 00:01:08.804
It finds the three pages that matter,
and proposes every measurement for

00:01:08.862 --> 00:01:13.413
the scaffold, each one beside the
line on the page it came from.

00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:17.036
So when the length reads 12.17,

00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:21.506
the estimator can see it's the
diagonal check, and puts 13.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.270
And everything follows.

00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:24.524
The perimeter.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.533
The metres per lift.

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:30.550
192.92 linear metres.

00:01:30.956 --> 00:01:34.230
£4,572.

00:01:34.776 --> 00:01:38.166
Where the drawing doesn't say,
like the corner allowance,

00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:43.146
or the render, it leaves the field
empty, and won't price until someone

00:01:43.204 --> 00:01:43.785
fills it.

00:01:44.423 --> 00:01:48.162
Type a length that makes
no sense, and it refuses.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.146
The rate band is a commercial call.

00:01:51.691 --> 00:01:55.790
Medium, or High at £5,710.

00:01:56.335 --> 00:01:57.984
That stays with the estimator.

00:01:58.274 --> 00:02:01.060
Then it writes the summary
for the estimating system.

00:02:01.606 --> 00:02:06.494
Every line, with its quantity,
its unit, and where it came from.

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:11.765
So every draft quote starts from
the drawing, and every figure traces

00:02:11.869 --> 00:02:12.728
back to it.

00:02:13.448 --> 00:02:14.632
The drawings arrive.

00:02:15.039 --> 00:02:16.339
The quote follows.
